ain"}, {"id": 48768664, "name": "metaspades_viral.fa", "size": 1229779299, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/48768664", "supplied_md5": "f72064ed99ca4779ab27825d7bd4c15c", "computed_md5": "f72064ed99ca4779ab27825d7bd4c15c", "mimetype": "text/plain"}, {"id": 48768649, "name": "metaviralspades_viral.fa", "size": 219800453, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/48768649", "supplied_md5": "673cb48ccbd5534c422c20589562ec12", "computed_md5": "673cb48ccbd5534c422c20589562ec12", "mimetype": "text/plain"}, {"id": 48768658, "name": "opera_viral.fa", "size": 1150392591, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/48768658", "supplied_md5": "ecc462f7c7f1b54a73b05207b95ceab2", "computed_md5": "ecc462f7c7f1b54a73b05207b95ceab2", "mimetype": "text/plain"}, {"id": 48768643, "name": "wtdbg2_viral.fa", "size": 6539512, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/48768643", "supplied_md5": "308783e412f4bcda3d865e91b6e393fc", "computed_md5": "308783e412f4bcda3d865e91b6e393fc", "mimetype": "text/plain"}, {"id": 48768805, "name": "megahit_viral.fa", "size": 1526657126, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/48768805", "supplied_md5": "f14a78dbd14f152a8f861f5b20b08df6", "computed_md5": "f14a78dbd14f152a8f861f5b20b08df6", "mimetype": "text/plain"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 13226766, "full_name": "Wei-Hua Chen", "first_name": "Wei-Hua", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Wei-Hua_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/Viral_contigs_of_Virome_Benchmark/25060193", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The VLP sequencing data were then assembled using the selected assemblers. Default parameters were used unless otherwise stated. Briefly, for the NGS data, we used IDBA-UD (v1.1.4), MEGAHIT (v1.2.9), and metaSPAdes (v3.15.4). For the TGS data, we selected Canu (v2.2), FALCON (v1.8.1), Hifiasm-meta (v0.3), metaFlye (v2.9.1), and wtdbg2 (v2.5). For hybrid assembly that combines the NGS and TGS data, we used IDBA-hyb (v1.1.3), hybridSPAdes (v3.15.4), metaViralSPAdes (v3.15.4) and OPERA-MS (v0.83).</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Dereplication was performed on contigs obtained by each tool on each sample or multi-tools on all samples using cd-hit (v4.6.8) with a parameter of -c 0.99 according to a previous study. Viral contigs were then identified using a similar procedure to human Gut Virome Database (GVD), with modifications. Briefly, the following virus recognition software were firstly used, including VirSorter2 (v2.2.4), DeepVirFinder (v1.0), VirFinder (v1.1), Seeker, and PPR-Meta (v1.1) . Their parameters were listed as the following. 1. VirSorter score \u2265 0.7, 2. DeepVirFinder pvalue<0.05, 3. VirFinder score > 0.6, 4. Seeker with the default parameter, 5. PPR-Meta phage score > 0.7. Secondly, a contig was considered as a virus if it passed at least two out the above five criteria and had sequence length >1.5kb.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 10623758945, "created_date": "2024-08-25T09:44:59Z", "modified_date": "2024-08-25T09:44:59Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["human gut virome", "Metagenomic Assembly", "viral contigs"], "keywords": ["human gut virome", "Metagenomic Assembly", "viral contigs"], "categories": [{"id": 24199, "title": "Sequence analysis", "parent_id": 24181, "path": "/24130/24181/24199", "source_id": "310206", "taxonomy_id": 100}], "references": [], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Chen, Wei-Hua (2024). Viral contigs of Virome Benchmark. figshare. Dataset.